{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And my servant Caleb.</b> There was no need to mention Joshua, because he was destined to bring them into the land. Another interpretation: he did not mention him because he had no sons, and one cannot say of him וזרעו יורשנה, 'and his seed shall inherit it.'" "<b>And he filled after me.</b> He completed the matter after Moses his emissary, so as to hold fast to him in imitation, as in 'and I will come after you and fulfill your words.'" "<b>And his seed shall inherit it.</b> An expression of inheritance, meaning: and to his seed — those who issue from his seed — he shall give it as an inheritance to the sons who come after them."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:56.838131623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}